rm{d}t\\\\ &= -3\\int t^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+5\\int t^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+4\\int t^{1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -3\\left(\\frac{t^{1}}{1}\\right)+5\\left(\\frac{t^{3}}{3}\\right)+4\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -3t+\\frac{5t^{3}}{3}+2t^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cee45ab3-b6a7-55bd-81d7-91cc0f754b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t-\\frac{t^{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cee45ab3-b6a7-55bd-81d7-91cc0f754b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t-\\frac{t^{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671262} :answer-field/id #uuid "6da02c21-1f30-53c9-880d-0cfa7b47976c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9214c456-0ded-5e8a-9e44-d24503d0acbe" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int 4-t^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int 4-t^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(4-t^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= 4\\int t^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-\\int t^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= 4\\left(\\frac{t^{1}}{1}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{t^{7}}{7}\\right)+C\\\\ &= 4t-\\frac{t^{7}}{7}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ab0ab0b-f131-5357-a68a-f9c57d76df0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\sqrt